14:\"dependencyType\";r:194;}}}}"},"\/app\/packages\/nexus-psalm\/src\/Hook\/BehaviorReceiveReturnTypeProvider.php":{"hash":"b3aa679c14d2b0c56e79de428d862537872888fa","reference":"O:49:\"Deptrac\\Deptrac\\Contract\\Ast\\AstMap\\FileReference\":4:{s:19:\"classLikeReferences\";a:1:{i:0;O:54:\"Deptrac\\Deptrac\\Contract\\Ast\\AstMap\\ClassLikeReference\":7:{s:62:\"\u0000Deptrac\\Deptrac\\Contract\\Ast\\AstMap\\TaggedTokenReference\u0000tags\";a:4:{s:10:\"@psalm-api\";a:1:{i:0;s:177:\"\n\nInfers `ReceiveBehavior<T>` from the message-parameter type of the\nhandler closure passed to `Behavior::receive(...)`.\n\nThe existing docblock on `Behavior::receive()` declares\";}s:9:\"@template\";a:1:{i:0;s:11:\"U of object\";}s:6:\"@param\";a:1:{i:0;s:49:\"Closure(ActorContext<U>, U): Behavior<U> $handler\";}s:7:\"@return\";a:1:{i:0;s:853:\"ReceiveBehavior<U> \n\nbut Psalm's template-from-closure-param inference doesn't reliably\npropagate U out \u2014 at the call site users see `ReceiveBehavior<object>`\neven when their closure takes a specific message type. This hook reads\nthe closure's second parameter type at the call site and rewrites the\nreturn to `ReceiveBehavior<MessageClass>`.\n\nExample:\n\n    $b = Behavior::receive(\n        static fn(ActorContext $ctx, GetOrder $msg): Behavior => Behavior::same(),\n    );\n    \/\/ Without hook: ReceiveBehavior<object>\n    \/\/ With hook:    ReceiveBehavior<GetOrder>\n\nThe hook only fires when the closure's second parameter is a single\nnamed class. The bare `object` keyword (parsed as TObject, rejected by\nthe `!instanceof TNamedObject` guard), unions, and untyped params all\nfall through to Psalm's default behavior (typically\nReceiveBehavior<object>).\";}}s:4:\"type\";E:60:\"Deptrac\\Deptrac\\Contract\\Ast\\AstMap\\ClassLikeType:TYPE_CLASS\";s:69:\"\u0000Deptrac\\Deptrac\\Contract\\Ast\\AstMap\\ClassLikeReference\u0000classLikeName\";O:50:\"Deptrac\\Deptrac\\Contract\\Ast\\AstMap\\ClassLikeToken\":1:{s:61:\"\u0000Deptrac\\Deptr