ac\\Contract\\Ast\\AstMap\\DependencyToken\":2:{s:5:\"token\";O:50:\"Deptrac\\Deptrac\\Contract\\Ast\\AstMap\\ClassLikeToken\":1:{s:61:\"\u0000Deptrac\\Deptrac\\Contract\\Ast\\AstMap\\ClassLikeToken\u0000className\";s:16:\"Psalm\\Type\\Union\";}s:7:\"context\";O:53:\"Deptrac\\Deptrac\\Contract\\Ast\\AstMap\\DependencyContext\":2:{s:14:\"fileOccurrence\";O:50:\"Deptrac\\Deptrac\\Contract\\Ast\\AstMap\\FileOccurrence\":2:{s:8:\"filepath\";s:74:\"\/app\/packages\/nexus-psalm\/src\/Hook\/BehaviorWithStateReturnTypeProvider.php\";s:4:\"line\";i:157;}s:14:\"dependencyType\";r:155;}}}s:4:\"tags\";a:4:{s:10:\"@psalm-api\";a:1:{i:0;s:156:\"\n\nInfers `WithStateBehavior<T, S>` from the handler closure passed to\n`Behavior::withState(...)`.\n\nThe existing docblock on `Behavior::withState()` declares\";}s:9:\"@template\";a:2:{i:0;s:11:\"U of object\";i:1;s:1:\"S\";}s:6:\"@param\";a:2:{i:0;s:15:\"S $initialState\";i:1;s:64:\"Closure(ActorContext<U>, U, S): BehaviorWithState<U, S> $handler\";}s:7:\"@return\";a:1:{i:0;s:788:\"WithStateBehavior<U, S> \n\nbut Psalm doesn't reliably back-propagate U\/S from the closure body, so\ncall sites see `WithStateBehavior<object, mixed>`. This hook extracts\nthe closure's second parameter (message type, U) and third parameter\n(state type, S) and rewrites the return to a properly narrowed generic.\n\nExample:\n\n    $b = Behavior::withState(\n        0,\n        static fn(ActorContext $ctx, Increment $msg, int $count) => ...,\n    );\n    \/\/ Without hook: WithStateBehavior<object, mixed>\n    \/\/ With hook:    WithStateBehavior<Increment, int>\n\nPartial inference is supported: a typed state with an `object` message\nstill returns `WithStateBehavior<object, int>` (narrower than the\ndefault). If the closure shape can't be inspected at all, the hook\nfalls through to Psalm's default.\";}}s:69:\"\u0000Deptrac\\Deptrac\\Contract\\Ast\\AstMap\\ClassLikeReference\u0000fileReference\";r:1;}}s:18:\"functionReferences\";a:0:{}s:8:\"filepath\";s:74