pPayloadCodec.php\";s:4:\"line\";i:10;}s:14:\"dependencyType\";r:146;}}}}"},"\/app\/packages\/nexus-cluster-tcp\/src\/Payload\/MsgpackReader.php":{"hash":"f41d23833db811f2a7bb0b7bdb72c15eab1bc032","reference":"O:49:\"Deptrac\\Deptrac\\Contract\\Ast\\AstMap\\FileReference\":4:{s:19:\"classLikeReferences\";a:1:{i:0;O:54:\"Deptrac\\Deptrac\\Contract\\Ast\\AstMap\\ClassLikeReference\":7:{s:62:\"\u0000Deptrac\\Deptrac\\Contract\\Ast\\AstMap\\TaggedTokenReference\u0000tags\";a:1:{s:10:\"@psalm-api\";a:1:{i:0;s:932:\"\n\nTyped, forward-compatible reader over an unpacked msgpack map, shared by the cluster's hand-rolled\ncontrol-frame codecs ({@see HandshakeCodec}, {@see HandshakeAckCodec}, {@see GossipPayloadCodec},\n{@see LeavePayloadCodec}). It exists so those codecs can stay off Valinor \u2014 the cluster wire\nprotocol is a fixed set of internal VOs on the hot gossip\/heartbeat path, where the mapper's\nreflection-driven hydration is pure overhead \u2014 while still validating every field taken off the\nnetwork before a VO is built.\n\nForward compatibility: fields are resolved BY KEY with sensible defaults, and unknown keys are\nignored, so a newer protocol version can add a field without breaking an older reader.\n\nTrust boundary: the bytes come straight off the wire. Every accessor type-checks and throws\n{@see MessageDeserializationException} on a mismatch, which frame ingress treats as an undecodable\nframe (dropped and counted, never routed).\";}}s:4:\"type\";E:60:\"Deptrac\\Deptrac\\Contract\\Ast\\AstMap\\ClassLikeType:TYPE_CLASS\";s:69:\"\u0000Deptrac\\Deptrac\\Contract\\Ast\\AstMap\\ClassLikeReference\u0000classLikeName\";O:50:\"Deptrac\\Deptrac\\Contract\\Ast\\AstMap\\ClassLikeToken\":1:{s:61:\"\u0000Deptrac\\Deptrac\\Contract\\Ast\\AstMap\\ClassLikeToken\u0000className\";s:48:\"Monadial\\Nexus\\Cluster\\Tcp\\Payload\\MsgpackReader\";}s:8:\"inherits\";a:0:{}s:12:\"dependencies\";a:24:{i:0;O:51:\"Deptrac\\Deptrac\\Contract\\Ast\\AstMap\\DependencyToken\":2:{s: